# AI Resume Analyzer — Project Spec

## Stack
- Frontend: React.js (Vite), Tailwind CSS, React Router, Axios, Recharts, Framer Motion (for animations)
- Backend: Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB + Mongoose, JWT + bcrypt
- AI: Google Gemini API (called only from backend, key in .env, never exposed to frontend)
- File parsing: pdf-parse (PDF) and mammoth (DOCX)
- PDF report generation: pdfkit or puppeteer

## Pages (Frontend)
1. Home (landing page, marketing-style, professional theme)
2. Login / Register (JWT auth, protected routes after login)
3. Dashboard (overview: recent analyses, quick stats, upload CTA)
4. Resume Upload (drag-and-drop PDF/DOCX upload)
5. Resume Analysis (shows ATS score, skills, missing skills, keywords,
   missing keywords, strengths, weaknesses, grammar/formatting suggestions,
   improvement suggestions — as charts via Recharts + text)
6. Job Matching (paste Job Description, matches against a chosen resume,
   shows: match % out of 10 "should I apply" score, missing skills,
   expected salary range based on JD, what to add/learn)
7. Profile (user info, change password)
8. Analysis History (list of past resume analyses + job matches, with PDF report download)

## Backend APIs
- POST /api/auth/register
- POST /api/auth/login
- GET  /api/auth/me
- POST /api/resume/upload         (multipart upload, extract text, store in DB)
- POST /api/resume/analyze/:id    (calls Gemini, returns ATS score + full breakdown)
- POST /api/jobmatch/:resumeId    (body: jobDescription text; calls Gemini, returns match score)
- GET  /api/history                (list past analyses for logged-in user)
- GET  /api/history/:id/pdf        (generate & download PDF report)

## Database Models (Mongoose)
- User: name, email, passwordHash, createdAt
- Resume: userId, fileName, extractedText, uploadedAt
- Analysis: userId, resumeId, atsScore, skills[], missingSkills[], keywords[],
  missingKeywords[], strengths[], weaknesses[], suggestions[], createdAt
- JobMatch: userId, resumeId, jobDescription, matchScore (out of 10),
  missingSkills[], expectedSalaryRange, recommendations[], createdAt

## AI Output Requirements (Gemini prompt must request structured JSON with):
- atsScore (0–100)
- skills (array)
- missingSkills (array)
- keywords (array)
- missingKeywords (array)
- strengths (array)
- weaknesses (array)
- grammarSuggestions (array)
- improvementSuggestions (array)
- (for job matching) matchScore (0–10), missingSkillsForJob (array),
  expectedSalaryRange (string), recommendation (string: "Apply" / "Improve first" / "Not a fit")

## UI/Design requirements
- Professional theme (not playful) — deep blue/indigo or slate + white,
  clean sans-serif (Inter or similar)
- Framer Motion for page transitions and subtle element animations
  (fade/slide on load, animated score counters, animated progress bars for ATS score)
- Recharts for score visualizations (radial/gauge chart for ATS score,
  bar chart for skill match)
- Fully responsive, mobile-friendly
- Loading skeletons while AI analysis runs (this can take a few seconds)

## Security
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt
- JWT stored in httpOnly cookie or Authorization header
- Gemini API key only in backend .env, never sent to frontend
- Input validation on all endpoints
